clean_summary:
Excited to share Sim2Reason — training LLMs in simulation to learn Olympiad-level physics (mechanics). Today, LLMs learn science by reading what humans have already written, but human-annotated physics data is scarce, and that bottleneck isn't going away.

Sim2Reason makes the same bet as Sim2Real in robotics — skip the descriptions and let models learn directly from simulated worlds, observing how objects move, collide, and interact. Models trained purely on simulated experience develop transferable physical reasoning skills, improving even on problems they never saw during training, achieving zero-shot gains on IPhO, IIT JEE Advanced, and OlympiadBench.

@mihirp98: "What if AI learned physics the way Newton did – by experiencing it? We built Sim2Reason: train LLMs inside virtual worlds governed by real physics laws, zero human annotation. Result: +5–10% improvement on International Physics Olympiad, zero-shot."

Update: This work has been accepted at ICML. We’ve also released our code, model weights, dataset, and all resources here.

